end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186120522 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=-12 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=-10 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+24\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+24.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+24\\,⇒\\,k=-24.\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186124483 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342034 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186124483 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342036 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186124483 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342037 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186124484 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342038 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186124484 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342039 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186124484 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342041 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186124485 1038 #edb/ref 