42116 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342116 1071 "Find $x$, if $3a+2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342116 1072 #uuid "0a045a18-4b26-532b-8e6c-7d683732c9ac" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342116 1074 "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342117 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341572 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342117 1069 "q-73933" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342117 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342117 1071 "Find $x$, if $5a-3x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 18 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342117 1072 #uuid "3b51a337-e5d6-556d-a72d-bef903a48688" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342117 1074 "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-3x & =b \\\\ 3x & =5a-b \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(5a-b) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(5[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 18 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 51\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342118 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341814 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342118 1069 "q-73939" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342118 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342118 1071 "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ What is $(\\frac{1}{2}a)\\cdot b?$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342118 1072 #uuid "7fa0bdb5-f053-5d67-8f95-d145fa39b1e1" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342118 1074 "First, multiplying each component of $a$ by $\\frac{1}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}a & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{2}a)\\cdot b & =2\\cdot 5+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =10+3+1+0+10 \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342119 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341721 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342119 1069 "q-73941" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342119 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342119 1071 "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ What is $(-\\frac{1}{3}c)\\cdot d?$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342119 1072 #uuid "9d756465-9173-5daf-942c-7abdf0168d3c" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342119 1074 "First, multiplying each component of $c$ by $-\\frac{1}{3}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}c & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{1}{3}c)\\cdot d & =0\\cdot 9+2\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =0+8+8-3-6 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342120 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341461 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342120 1069 "q-73948" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342120 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342120 1071 "Let $v=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 2x \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}3x \\\\ -3 \\\\ x \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\nIf $v\\cdot w=-2$ and $x>0$, find the value of $x.$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342120 1072 #uuid "e030b11b-7d8c-5bb3-95d3-2268959b30a1" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342120 1074 "Starting from the equation $v\\cdot w=-2,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot w & =-2 \\\\ x\\cdot 3x+2x\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot x+(-5)\\cdot 2 & =-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-6x+4x-10 & =-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(3)(-8)}}{2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{100}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 10}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{4}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ Since we need $x>0$, our final answer is $x=2$ only." 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342121 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341689 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342121 1069 "q-73949" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342121 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342121 1071 "Let $l=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ x \\\\ 2 \\\\ x \\\\ 2x\\end{aligned}]$ and $m=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ x \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$\nIf $l\\cdot m=3$ and $x>3$, find the value of $x.$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342121 1072 #uuid "64baab11-7178-5faa-a751-966ea0fbee6f" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342121 1074 "Starting from the equation $l\\cdot m=3,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l\\cdot m & =3 \\\\ 5\\cdot 1+x\\cdot x+2\\cdot 4+x\\cdot (-1)+2x\\cdot (-3) & =3 \\\\ 5+{x}^{2}+8-x-6x & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-7x+13 & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-7x+10 & =0 \\\\ (x-5)(x-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ Since we need $x>3$, our final answer is $x=5$ only." 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342122 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341612 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342122 1069 "q-73951" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342122 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342122 1071 "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$\n." 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342122 1072 #uuid "0008ebd1-cf28-5d38-a9cd-5c6dde0f95a6" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342122 1074 "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-11 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the second and the third  equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1} & =-16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ into the third equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-2)+{x}_{2}=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =3 \\\\ (-2)+2(3) & =3 \\\\ 4 & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution." 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342123 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341751 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342123 1069 "q-73952" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342123 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342123 1071 "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342123 1072 #uuid "eec4fe83-c254-5d51-9484-b88391578898" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342123 1074 "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-7 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equation we get\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}=-8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{2}=4$ into the first equation yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1}-(4) & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-7+4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =6 \\\\ 2(-3)+3(4) & =6 \\\\ 6 & =6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3+4=1.\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342124 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341737 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342124 1069 "q-73954" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342124 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342124 1071 "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342124 1072 #uuid "abf235b3-2d59-5bfb-aea0-aa237461f6b8" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342124 1074 "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=16 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$, the second equation by $2$, and adding the resulting equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{x}_{2}+8{x}_{2} & =48-2 \\\\ 23{x}_{2} & =46 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=2$  into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & =-1\\text{ } \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4(2) & =-1 \\\\ 3{x}_{1} & =-9 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=2$ into our third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} & =-18 \\\\ 4(-3)-3(2) & =-18 \\\\ -18 & =-18,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-3)+2=-1.\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342125 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341539 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342125 1069 "q-73955" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342125 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342125 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342125 1072 #uuid "8e8fc794-8de1-566d-a7d1-0246dc2589a9" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342125 1074 "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+y-2z=-5 \\\\ 0x+2y-2z=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-5,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution." 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342126 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341412 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342126 1069 "q-73958" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342126 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342126 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342126 1072 #uuid "b176b3fe-cf93-51c6-8ce9-e7905742c0c0" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342126 1074 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -12 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -12 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 34\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-6z=8 \\\\ 0x-y-12z=16 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=34,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution." 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342127 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341790 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342127 1069 "q-73959" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342127 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342127 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -12 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 