orm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -12 & -6 & 16 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2 & 5 & 12 \\\\ 2 & -20 & -4 & 25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -12 & -6 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -20 & -4 & 25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -12 & -6 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -12 & -6 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -12 & -6 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-12y-6z=16 \\\\ 0x+y+2z=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-11,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution." 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342129 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341632 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342129 1069 "q-73981" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342129 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342129 1071 "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342129 1072 #uuid "3c67076c-502b-504a-869c-d6e3549e0a05" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342129 1074 "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the third equation by $-1$ and adding the result to the first equation we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{1} & =7-4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow,  we substitute ${x}_{1}=3$ into the third equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 3(3)-{x}_{2} & =4 \\\\ -{x}_{2} & =4-9 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=5$ into the second equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =9 \\\\ -2(3)+3(5) & =9 \\\\ -6+15 & =9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=5,$ which means\n\n$$\n3{a}_{1}+5{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+5=8.\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342130 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341406 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342130 1069 "q-73985" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342130 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342130 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,0,2⟩+t⟨3,2,-3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩=6.\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342130 1072 #uuid "b7b7455d-19c2-5862-8ffa-6bf81d08e53f" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342130 1074 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ ⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ 5(2+3t)-2(2t)+3(2-3t) & =6 \\\\ 10+15t-4t+6-9t & =6 \\\\ 2t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+3(-5),2(-5),2-3(-5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-13,-10,17⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-13,-10,17).$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342131 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341592 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342131 1069 "q-73987" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342131 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342131 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨5,2,-4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩=36.\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342131 1072 #uuid "a27e98ee-3a96-559d-b75b-2bf4d0ce11d7" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342131 1074 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ ⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ 2(1+5t)-3(1+2t)+5(1-4t) & =36 \\\\ 2+10t-3-6t+5-20t & =36 \\\\ -16t & =32 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+5(-2),1+2(-2),1-4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-9,-3,9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-9,-3,9).$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342132 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341621 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342132 1069 "q-73992" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342132 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342132 1071 "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342132 1072 #uuid "33debd45-f90c-578d-9c6b-11c54937ac6b" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342132 1074 "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-5 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=-10 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2.5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2.5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-5 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2.5\\,{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2.5(-2)=8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=8-5=3.\n$$\n\nFinally,  substituting ${x}_{2}=3$ and ${x}_{3}=-2$  into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(3)+2(-2)=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=3$, and ${x}_{3}=-2,$ which means \n\n$$\n2{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}-2{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+3-2=3.\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342133 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341485 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342133 1069 "q-73993" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342133 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342133 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=2-3t \\\\ z=-2-6t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x-2y+4z-132=0.\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342133 1072 #uuid "8a17e320-306c-50fa-b84b-f8cbe958e629" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342133 1074 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y+4z-132 & =0 \\\\ 5(3-5t)-2(2-3t)+4(-2-6t) & =132 \\\\ 15-25t-4+6t-8-24t & =132 \\\\ -43t & =129 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5(-3)=18 \\\\ y=2-3(-3)=11 \\\\ z=-2-6(-3)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(18,11,16).$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342134 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341415 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342134 1069 "q-74003" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342134 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342134 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=5-t \\\\ y=4+2t \\\\ z=-6-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+6y-3z-130=0.\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342134 1072 #uuid "8d4d8f0f-1eab-5bd0-8f71-a26637e6257d" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342134 1074 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+6y-3z-130 & =0 \\\\ 4(5-t)+6(4+2t)-3(-6-3t) & =130 \\\\ 20-4t+24+12t+18+9t & =130 \\\\ 17t & =68 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-4=1 \\\\ y=4+2(4)=12 \\\\ z=-6-3(4)=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(1,12,-18).$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342135 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341644 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342135 1069 "q-74004" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342135 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342135 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-5,4,2⟩+s⟨0,3,1⟩+t⟨2,0,1⟩.\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342135 1072 #uuid "156769fc-4325-56fe-a6f3-a488d1baa118" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342135 1074 "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨0,3,1⟩\\times ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =3i+2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =⟨-5,4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ ⟨3-2w,1-5w,5+4w⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 3(3-2w)+2(1-5w)-6(5+4w) & =-19 \\\\ 9-6w+2-10w-30-24w & =-19 \\\\ -40w & =0 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=0$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨3-2(0),1-5(0),5+4(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(3,1,5).$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342136 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341763 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342136 1069 "q-74006" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342136 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342136 1071 "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342136 1072 #uuid "ff5142a4-ab7b-5300-baa5-14f6253ed7fa" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186