0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=5.$ Substituting this value in the second and first equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{2}-2(5)=-6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=4 \\\\  & {x}_{1}+5=8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=3$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=5,$ which means \n\n$$\n3{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}+5{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3+4+5=12.\n$$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342145 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341655 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342145 1069 "q-74049" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342145 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342145 1071 "Suppose $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $a\\cdot a<0$\n- $b\\cdot a=a\\cdot a$\n- $b\\cdot a<0$" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342145 1072 #uuid "ec2dfaf1-eafb-5d88-8d0f-be9d2909829b" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342145 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $a\\ne 0$, we must have $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement II is false while statement III is true. Simplifying the expression $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a+b\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-a\\cdot a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0$, we obtain that $-a\\cdot a<0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342146 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341555 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342146 1069 "q-74051" 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [17592186342146 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533427 17592186045585 true] [175921863